.TH XIL\-SFX\-RESTORE "1" "2026\-07\-09" "xil\-pipeline 0.3.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xil\-sfx\-restore
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xil\-sfx\-restore
[-h] (--episode EPISODE | --tag TAG) [--show SHOW] [--sfx SFX] [--dry-run]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reapply journaled timeline sound edits (sfx_<tag>_edits.jsonl) onto the episode's SFX config — recovery for a cleared or regenerated sfx_<tag>.json.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-episode\fR \fI\,EPISODE\/\fR
Episode tag (e.g. S04E04)

.TP
\fB\-\-tag\fR \fI\,TAG\/\fR
Raw non\-episodic tag (e.g. V01C03)

.TP
\fB\-\-show\fR \fI\,SHOW\/\fR
Show name override (default: from project.json)

.TP
\fB\-\-sfx\fR \fI\,SFX\/\fR
Override SFX config path

.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Report what would be reapplied without writing

